-- The cross-IMPORT refusal (`export-refused.l4`, §11.19 OF-7) for an export whose
-- INPUT DEFAULT reaches the imported reader, which is a way round it that the
-- check on the body alone left open (W7, R8 rule 3: a default is an expression).
--
-- `implicit-rate-lib` declares a section GIVEN `the rate` and a rule that reads
-- it. The export's own input `markup` takes a default that calls that rule, so a
-- request that leaves `markup` out reaches an imported reader exactly as a body
-- that called it would. Discharge does not cross an IMPORT, so it runs out as an
-- internal error ("running bin op with invalid operation") and not as an
-- answer. It is refused at check time instead.

IMPORT `implicit-rate-lib`

@export What this amount comes to with a markup that defaults to the rate on 100.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      markup IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (`scaled by the rate` 100)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cost with markup` MEANS amount PLUS markup
